# A discrete uniform draw over three values has mean exactly 1, so this upper bound is false.
# Expected: unknown (the bound checker proves bounds and never refutes one).
# A sampler that weighted each value by 1/3 at every nesting level instead gave the
# distribution 4/9, 2/9, 1/3 on 0, 1, 2, whose mean 8/9 is below 0.9, and the false bound
# could be proved.
x ~ UniformDisc(0, 3);
return x
?Ex[x] <= 0.9
